## Features & Traits

### Racial Traits

- **Draconic Ancestry (Red):** Breath weapon and damage resistance keyed to fire.
- **Breath Weapon(1/1 uses):** 15-ft cone, 4d6 fire damage (3d6 natural at level 6 + 1d6 Ascension Stage 1), DEX save DC 14 for half. Resets on a short or long rest.
- **Damage Resistance:** Resistance to fire damage.
- **Darkvision 60 ft** (new, Ascension Stage 1 — dragonborn don't naturally have this).
- **Languages:** Common, Draconic.

### Ascension — Draconic Awakening

**Stage 1** (day 73, session 17 — 3 fragments held, level 7 crossed): +1 AC (in Combat Stats above), Darkvision 60 ft, Breath Weapon +1d6 over natural progression (in Attacks above). **Cost — hoard-sense**: cannot make himself sell, gift, or abandon anything he considers his own. DC 12 WIS save to voluntarily part with something of value — play as roleplay first, dice only if he pushes. See `info/ascension-tracks.md`.

**First real test, day 74, session 17**: paying out 330 gp to Dallin Marsh for the garrison recruitment plan — a real, felt resistance, but the DC 12 WIS save succeeded (15+1=16). Passed cleanly, no complication.

**Two more tests, day 81, session 17** (resolved retroactively after being missed live — see `bug-log.md`, `workflow-skip`): giving Alis Wend 20 gp (15+1=16, success) and giving Roskel 1,000 gp for household expenses (14+1=15, success). Both passed — three for three so far.

### Class Features

- **Extra Attack (level 5):** Attacks twice, instead of once, whenever he takes the Attack action on his turn.
- **Fighting Style — Great Weapon Fighting:** When rolling a 1 or 2 on a damage die from a melee weapon held in two hands, reroll the die once and use the new roll.
- **Second Wind(0/1 uses):** Bonus action to regain 1d10 + fighter level (5) HP. Resets on a short or long rest. Gained level 2.
- **Action Surge(0/1 uses):** On his turn, take one additional action. Resets on a short or long rest. Gained level 2.
- **Martial Archetype — Battle Master** (gained level 3; not in the free SRD, applied from standard published rules — flagged in `system-register.md`):
  - **Combat Superiority — Superiority Dice(2/5 uses):** d8s. **+1 die at level 7 (was 4).** Spend one to fuel a maneuver; regain all on a short or long rest. Maneuver save DC 15 (8 + prof 3 + STR mod 4, updated for level 5's proficiency increase).
  - **Maneuvers known**: **Goading Attack** (hit: target has disadvantage on attacks against anyone but Kriv until end of his next turn, WIS save negates), **Precision Attack** (add the die to an attack roll, before or after the roll), **Distracting Strike** (hit: next ally's attack roll against that target has advantage), **Bait and Switch** (new, level 7 — he and a willing creature within 5 ft swap places; add the die as a bonus to his or the ally's AC until the start of his next turn, no attack roll involved), **Lunging Attack** (new, level 7 — when making a melee weapon attack, gain 5 ft of extra reach for that attack; if it hits, add the die to the damage).
  - **Student of War:** proficiency with smith's tools.
  - **Know Your Enemy** (gained level 7; not in the free SRD, applied from standard published rules): if he spends at least 1 minute observing or interacting with a creature outside combat, the DM tells him whether that creature is his equal, superior, or inferior in two of the following, his choice: Strength score, Dexterity score, Constitution score, Armor Class, current HP, total class levels, Fighter class levels.

### Background Feature

- **Position of Privilege:** Welcomed in high society; commoners try to avoid making trouble for him. May be able to secure audiences with nobles/officials.

### Feats

- **Great Weapon Master** (taken level 6, in place of an ASI; not in the free SRD, applied from standard published rules — flagged in `system-register.md`). No prerequisite.
  - Once on your turn when you score a critical hit with a melee weapon, or reduce a creature to 0 HP with one, you can make one melee weapon attack as a bonus action.
  - Before making a melee attack with a **heavy** weapon you're proficient with, you can choose to take a -5 penalty to the attack roll; if it hits, add +10 to the damage. **The Barrow-King's Blade qualifies** (a greataxe, Heavy property) — declare the -5/+10 before rolling each attack it applies to.

