*(Kobold tunnel-map fragment and the cistern sabotage diagram discarded, session 6 — Kargrim's Reach is fully resolved, no further use for either.)*

- **Wardensteel** — the house blade, taken from the kneeling effigy in Shestendeliath Hold's oath-hall (session 9, day 51). A magic longsword (versatile — Great Weapon Fighting applies two-handed), currently **+1 to attack and damage rolls only**. Carries the house arms at the hilt and an unfinished rune band — per `kriv-thread.md`, this unlocks into a full **Flame Tongue** (+2d6 fire, bonus-action ignite, 40 ft bright/40 ft dim light) as Kriv actually reclaims the house; not yet unlocked. **Requires attunement — not yet attuned** (would need to free a slot from Barrow-King's Blade/Cloak of Elvenkind/Amulet of Proof against Detection and Location, all 3/3 currently in use). Carried, not wielded, until that decision is made.
- **The Barrow-King's Blade** — recovered from the deep barrow at Hollowmoor (session 4), taken from the sarcophagus after the Warden's defeat. Ash-king era, grey-fire, reskinned as a greataxe (mechanically a Sun Blade). +2 to attack/damage, deals radiant instead of slashing, +1d8 radiant vs undead, can shed bright/dim light (bonus action, 15-30 ft). **Attuned** the last camp night before Harrowgate (session 4, day 27-28) — now his primary weapon; the mundane Greataxe is carried as a backup. 1 of 3 attunement slots used. **Carry method, added session 10 (day 52)**: after both Corvin Thale and a Harrowgate blacksmith recognized the blade on sight (session 4) — the exact identifying-weapon risk `new-capabilities.md` already flagged — Kriv now straps it across his back, hidden under whatever he's wearing over it, only the hilt visible. Drawn from there when needed. Not a mechanical change (still his primary weapon, same stats), just how he carries it in public now.
- **Cloak of Elvenkind** — bought from Corvin Thale at the Sable Casket, Harrowgate (session 4), haggled from 250 gp to 200 gp (Persuasion 22). Hood up: advantage on Stealth checks to hide, disadvantage on Perception checks made to see him. **Attuned** same visit, in Corvin's back room. 2 of 3 attunement slots used. **Standing default (DM-confirmed 2026-09-02): the hood stays up at all times unless the DM explicitly says otherwise for a scene** — don't ask each time, assume up.
- **Amulet of Proof against Detection and Location** — bought at the Ashgate Conservatory, Harrowgate (session 8, day 51, 500 gp). **Attuned** (session 9, day 51, same short rest that ended the Periapt's attunement). While worn, hidden from divination magic — can't be targeted by it or perceived through a magical scrying sensor. 3 of 3 attunement slots used (Barrow-King's Blade, Cloak of Elvenkind, Amulet).
  - **[DM: new-capabilities.md intake]** — not identifying (it conceals, doesn't mark him), no noise/light/witnesses/physical evidence. **Directly relevant to the live Concordat search**: Sarelle's unnamed investigator (`consequences.md`'s Convergence Risk) would need a scrying-based method to ever locate Kriv specifically while this is worn — a real, standing counter to that thread, not just flavor. Doesn't touch the ascension tracks.
- **1 light warhorse** — bought in Harrowgate (session 3), unbranded, clean.
- **2 Concordat holy symbols** and **a sealed Concordat transport manifest** (Order No. 447-C) — looted from the ambushed convoy (session 3). Kept as trophies/evidence, not sold.
- **Draconic-script "treasure map"** — bought from a Harrowgate mapmaker (session 3, 5 gp), read by Kriv himself (Draconic). Pointed to the Harpy Crags; that site has been cleared and looted. Kept as a memento — its lead is spent.

